{
    "map": {
        "append_option.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how control points will be appended to the control point table.</p><ul><li><span title=\"ALL\">Add all points</span>—Add all points in the input control point table to the target control point table, including GCPs, check points, and all tie points. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"GCP\">Add GCPs only</span>—Add only GCPs in the input point table to the target control point table.</li><li><span title=\"GCPSET\">Add GCPs and tie points</span>—Add GCPs and tie points specifically associated with the GCPs to the target control point table.<p>Use caution with this option—it is applicable only when the tie points in the input and target control point table have the same transformation. The tie points might not be in the desired positions if they were computed using a different adjustment process.</p></li></ul></xdoc>",
        "append_option.domain.ALL": "Add all points",
        "append_option.domain.GCP": "Add GCPs only",
        "append_option.domain.GCPSET": "Add GCPs and tie points",
        "append_option.title": "Append Option",
        "area_of_interest.descr": "Defines an area of interest extent by entering minimum and maximum x- and y-coordinates in the spatial reference of the input control point table.",
        "area_of_interest.title": "Area of Interest",
        "description": "Combines control points to an existing control point table.",
        "geoid.descr": "<xdoc><p>The geoid correction is required by rational polynomial coefficients (RPC) that reference ellipsoidal heights. Most elevation datasets are referenced to sea level orthometric heights, so this correction would be required in these cases to convert to ellipsoidal heights.</p><ul><li>Unchecked—No geoid correction is made. Use this option only if your DEM is already expressed in ellipsoidal heights. This is the default.</li><li>Checked—A geoid correction will be made to convert orthometric heights to ellipsoidal heights (based on EGM96 geoid).</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "geoid.title": "Geoid",
        "in_dem.descr": "<xdoc><p>A DEM to use to obtain the z-value for the control points in the input control point table.</p><p>If both the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Z Value Field Name</span> and <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input DEM</span> parameters are set, the Z value field is used. If neither the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Z Value Field Name</span> nor the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input DEM</span> parameter is set, the z-value is set to 0 for all ground control points and check points.</p></xdoc>",
        "in_dem.title": "Input DEM",
        "in_input_control_points.descr": "A point feature class that stores control points. It could be the control point table created from the Compute Control Points tool, the Compute Tie Points tool, or a point feature class that has ground control points.",
        "in_input_control_points.title": "Input Control Points",
        "in_master_control_points.descr": "The input control point table. This is usually the output from the Compute Tie Points tool.",
        "in_master_control_points.title": "Target Control Points",
        "in_tag_field.descr": "A field in the input control point table that has a unique value. This field will be added to the target control point table, where the tag field can be used to bring in identifiers associated with ground control points.",
        "in_tag_field.title": "Tag Field Name",
        "in_xy_accuracy.descr": "<xdoc><p>The input accuracy for the X and Y coordinates. The accuracy is in the same units as the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Control Points</span>.</p><p>This information should be provided by the data provider. If the accuracy information is not available, leave this optional parameter blank.</p></xdoc>",
        "in_xy_accuracy.title": "XY Accuracy",
        "in_z_accuracy.descr": "<xdoc><p>The input accuracy for the vertical coordinates. The accuracy is in the units of the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Control Points</span>.</p><p>This information should be provided by the data provider. If the accuracy information is not available, leave this optional parameter blank.</p></xdoc>",
        "in_z_accuracy.title": "Z Accuracy",
        "in_z_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>The field that stores the control point z-values.</p><p>If both the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Z Value Field Name</span> and the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input DEM</span> parameters are set, the Z value field is used. If neither the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Z Value Field Name</span> nor the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input DEM</span> parameter is set, the z-value is set to 0 for all ground control points and check points.</p></xdoc>",
        "in_z_field.title": "Z Value Field Name",
        "out_master_control_points.title": "Updated Control Points",
        "summary": "<xdoc><p>Combines control points to an existing control point table.</p><p>The points to be appended are the results from either the Compute Tie Points tool or the Compute Control Points tool, or a point feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "title": "Append Control Points"
    }
}
